WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.535
Hi, I'm Neymar Odaner and this is module 7 of OS

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:04.240
Work.

3
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.615
In the last module, you learned to save versions of your

4
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.480
work with Git, so nothing gets lost.

5
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.535
Now, we're going to find a way to talk to a

6
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.780
program of yours from your phone, using Telegram.

7
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.335
By the end of this module, you'll have a bot of

8
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.735
your own, created on Telegram, with its key kept in a

9
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.395
place nobody sees, serving only the people you've authorized, and

10
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.980
answering two lookup commands without executing any message.

11
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.215
You'll also know where an AI could come in without messing

12
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.255
up the numbers and how to test everything before you trust

13
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:36.520
it.

14
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.295
Denise and Lucia are still with us.

15
00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.355
Lucia is going to build a bot for the Grammys fictional

16
00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.515
school shop.

17
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.575
Each lesson has a short practice.

18
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.020
When I ask, pause the video and do it right then.

19
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.355
Let's start by separating two things that usually get mixed up.

20
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.655
When you chat with a bot on Telegram, the app on

21
00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.715
your phone only carries your message and brings the reply back.

22
00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.415
The one that reads, decides and replies is a program running

23
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.255
on your computer.

24
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.435
Think of the intercom at the gatehouse.

25
00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:07.864
The device carries the voice, but the person inside is the

26
00:01:07.889 --> 00:01:09.564
one who opens the gate.

27
00:01:09.589 --> 00:01:12.544
Denise heard that another school had an agent on Telegram.

28
00:01:12.569 --> 00:01:15.444
She asked what it did and found out it was three

29
00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:17.669
canned replies with no AI at all.

30
00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:20.784
The name promised more than the thing delivered.

31
00:01:20.809 --> 00:01:22.984
So keep this division in mind.

32
00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:26.224
Telegram receives what you write and delivers the reply in the

33
00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:27.084
same chat.

34
00:01:27.109 --> 00:01:31.944
Your program checks who wrote and which command it is, executes

35
00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:35.284
only the allowed function, and builds the reply.

36
00:01:35.309 --> 00:01:38.524
Both parts are needed, but only one decides.

37
00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:41.544
The bot in the course kit has two work commands and

38
00:01:41.569 --> 00:01:42.884
neither uses AI.

39
00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:45.964
The status command confirms it's running.

40
00:01:45.989 --> 00:01:50.864
The relatorial command, which means report, adds up three fictional

41
00:01:50.889 --> 00:01:56.444
sales from a file called vendas.csv, a spreadsheet in plain text.

42
00:01:56.469 --> 00:02:00.344
Lúcia will use this bot to check on the Grammys shop,

43
00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:02.329
notebook, pen and planner.

44
00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:05.104
She sends a relatório and the bot replies that there were

45
00:02:05.129 --> 00:02:07.484
three sales totaling 100 reais.

46
00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:11.174
That total comes from a calculation the program makes, not from

47
00:02:11.199 --> 00:02:12.059
a guess.

48
00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.379
That's what deterministic means.

49
00:02:14.619 --> 00:02:17.279
The same request always gets the same reply.

50
00:02:18.279 --> 00:02:20.159
And there's one more important detail.

51
00:02:20.359 --> 00:02:23.239
Whoever writes on Telegram doesn't control the computer.

52
00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:26.754
The bot compares the message with a short list of known

53
00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:30.579
commands, and everything else gets the same standard reply.

54
00:02:31.199 --> 00:02:31.494
Unknown command.

55
00:02:31.519 --> 00:02:34.674
That goes even for the bot's owner.

56
00:02:34.699 --> 00:02:40.014
Denise imagined a school office bot that received the sentence, delete

57
00:02:40.039 --> 00:02:41.419
yesterday's absences.

58
00:02:42.139 --> 00:02:45.794
With a closed list of commands, that sentence comes back as

59
00:02:45.819 --> 00:02:48.474
a known command and nothing is deleted.

60
00:02:48.499 --> 00:02:51.794
That's why, before you think about AI, you draw the whole

61
00:02:51.819 --> 00:02:53.339
path of a message.

62
00:02:53.399 --> 00:02:55.994
Then you mark the step where it would really help.

63
00:02:56.019 --> 00:02:57.819
A good candidate is the function.

64
00:02:57.859 --> 00:03:00.079
It could gain a text summary built from the numbers.

65
00:03:00.699 --> 00:03:01.594
The rule is firm.

66
00:03:01.619 --> 00:03:05.634
The number stays the program's number.

67
00:03:05.659 --> 00:03:07.994
Lucia marked that step.

68
00:03:08.019 --> 00:03:11.274
The AI could write that the planner was the biggest sale

69
00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:14.394
as long as the 100 reais total stays exactly as the

70
00:03:14.419 --> 00:03:16.374
program calculated it.

71
00:03:16.399 --> 00:03:17.703
Now pause the video.

72
00:03:17.728 --> 00:03:21.603
On paper, draw five boxes in a row.

73
00:03:21.628 --> 00:03:25.803
Phone, Telegram, Bot, Allowed Function and Reply.

74
00:03:25.828 --> 00:03:28.723
Under each one, write who does the work.

75
00:03:28.748 --> 00:03:31.543
Put an X in a single box and write what the

76
00:03:31.568 --> 00:03:34.323
AI would do there without changing numbers.

77
00:03:34.348 --> 00:03:37.823
Every Telegram bot is born in a chat with Botfather.

78
00:03:37.848 --> 00:03:40.163
You send the new bot command, choose a name and a

79
00:03:40.188 --> 00:03:42.883
username, and it gives you back the bot's token.

80
00:03:42.908 --> 00:03:46.943
The username has to end in bot, like Lojinha Grêmio Lúcia

81
00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:51.083
Bot, and if it's already taken, Botfather asks for another one.

82
00:03:51.108 --> 00:03:54.283
The token is a string of numbers, a column, and letters.

83
00:03:54.308 --> 00:03:56.383
It works like the key to the school gate.

84
00:03:56.408 --> 00:03:59.883
Whoever has a copy gets in, whoever they are.

85
00:03:59.908 --> 00:04:02.323
Lúcia created the shop bot in three messages.

86
00:04:02.348 --> 00:04:05.723
But first, she checked something important, that she was talking to

87
00:04:05.748 --> 00:04:10.823
the official Botfather with the blue verified badge and not to

88
00:04:10.848 --> 00:04:12.468
an account with a similar name.

89
00:04:13.368 --> 00:04:14.708
A practical detail.

90
00:04:14.908 --> 00:04:16.963
Botfather replies in English.

91
00:04:16.988 --> 00:04:19.803
And notice that in the lesson, the token is hidden on

92
00:04:19.828 --> 00:04:20.768
purpose.

93
00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:23.292
That's the same care you're going to take with yours.

94
00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.180
Where do you keep that key?

95
00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:30.595
In the bot folder, the course kit includes an example file .env.example,

96
00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.100
with only fake values.

97
00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.680
You make a copy called .env and paste the token inside it.

98
00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.175
That file stays on your computer only.

99
00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:43.935
The token doesn't go into a screenshot, a message, or a

100
00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:44.580
shared document.

101
00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.135
Denise thought about putting the token in the school office's instructions

102
00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.220
document, so nobody would lose it.

103
00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:51.980
She changed her mind.

104
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.820
The document says where the file is, never the value.

105
00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.140
In the terminal, inside the kits.bot folder, it's four commands.

106
00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.715
Go into the folder, copy the example, restrict reading with Chmod

107
00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.315
600, and check with ls.

108
00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.455
Chmod 600 lets only your account read and change the file.

109
00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:14.995
The last line has to start with dash, r, w, and

110
00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:15.840
then only dashes.

111
00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:19.375
The first three commands show nothing when they work, and that's

112
00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:19.655
normal.

113
00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.215
If you get a message that the file doesn't exist, you're

114
00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:24.900
not in the right folder.

115
00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.435
Repeat the cd command with the path where you unzip the

116
00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:28.940
kit.

117
00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.075
And if the token shows up in a screenshot, a message

118
00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.240
or a document, treat it as leaked.

119
00:05:34.265 --> 00:05:38.820
In Botfather, send my bots, pick the bot, tap API token

120
00:05:38.845 --> 00:05:41.540
and then revoke current token.

121
00:05:41.565 --> 00:05:45.400
It generates a new token and the old one stops working.

122
00:05:45.425 --> 00:05:47.840
Then replace the value in the dot environment.

123
00:05:47.865 --> 00:05:51.460
In a meeting, Denise saw a colleague's screenshot with the token

124
00:05:51.485 --> 00:05:52.680
in plain view.

125
00:05:52.705 --> 00:05:55.900
She spoke up right away and the team revoked and replaced

126
00:05:55.925 --> 00:05:57.000
it in 10 minutes.

127
00:05:57.025 --> 00:05:58.725
Now pause the video.

128
00:05:58.845 --> 00:06:02.280
your bot in Botfather, run the four commands, check the permissions

129
00:06:02.305 --> 00:06:08.180
line, and with the command nano.environ, replace the placeholder text

130
00:06:08.205 --> 00:06:10.980
preentia localmente with your token.

131
00:06:11.005 --> 00:06:12.765
No screenshots.

132
00:06:12.965 --> 00:06:16.140
With the token stored, another question comes up.

133
00:06:16.165 --> 00:06:18.580
Who can talk to the bot?

134
00:06:18.605 --> 00:06:21.260
The token proves to Telegram that your program owns the bot,

135
00:06:21.285 --> 00:06:23.380
but it says nothing about who can talk to it.

136
00:06:23.405 --> 00:06:26.880
That's why the kit has a second control, the access list.

137
00:06:26.905 --> 00:06:30.100
It's like the list of who can pick up each student

138
00:06:30.125 --> 00:06:31.485
at the end of the school day.

139
00:06:32.865 --> 00:06:34.745
Denise explained it to the team this way.

140
00:06:34.905 --> 00:06:38.120
The key opens the gate and the pick up list says

141
00:06:38.145 --> 00:06:39.885
who takes each student home.

142
00:06:40.265 --> 00:06:43.885
They're two separate checks and one doesn't replace the other.

143
00:06:44.385 --> 00:06:47.525
Both live in the same .nv file.

144
00:06:47.991 --> 00:06:50.966
The token on the Telegram bot token line and the list

145
00:06:50.991 --> 00:06:53.526
on the allowed user IGS line.

146
00:06:53.551 --> 00:06:56.766
And that list doesn't store names.

147
00:06:56.791 --> 00:06:59.146
The name that shows up in the chat.

148
00:06:59.171 --> 00:07:01.926
A person can change whenever they want.

149
00:07:01.951 --> 00:07:05.866
The bot checks the numeric ID, the number Telegram gives each

150
00:07:05.891 --> 00:07:06.691
account.

151
00:07:07.931 --> 00:07:11.566
Lucia shows up on Telegram as luciasciencias.

152
00:07:11.591 --> 00:07:17.526
If she changes it to Professor Lucia, the bot still recognizes

153
00:07:17.551 --> 00:07:19.991
her, because her number is the same.

154
00:07:20.911 --> 00:07:24.211
To find your number, the kit has an identification-only mode.

155
00:07:24.871 --> 00:07:29.266
The command python3botpy with the identify option.

156
00:07:29.291 --> 00:07:31.826
In this mode, the bot doesn't reply to anything on your

157
00:07:31.851 --> 00:07:33.946
phone and doesn't execute any function.

158
00:07:33.971 --> 00:07:37.886
You send the start command in a private chat with the

159
00:07:37.911 --> 00:07:40.806
bot and the number shows up in the terminal on a

160
00:07:40.831 --> 00:07:43.966
line that says ID recebido, ID received.

161
00:07:43.991 --> 00:07:47.386
Then you copy the number and stop it with control C.

162
00:07:47.411 --> 00:07:50.886
The number you see here on screen is fictional, yours will

163
00:07:50.911 --> 00:07:51.846
be different.

164
00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:56.686
If the terminal doesn't show any number, check three things that

165
00:07:56.711 --> 00:08:00.771
you sent, start in a private chat, not in a group.

166
00:08:00.796 --> 00:08:06.011
That the token in the .env belongs to the right bot.

167
00:08:06.036 --> 00:08:09.691
And that identification mode was still running.

168
00:08:09.716 --> 00:08:14.251
Before replying, the program checks three things in this order.

169
00:08:14.276 --> 00:08:15.551
Is it a private chat?

170
00:08:15.576 --> 00:08:17.731
If it's a group, silence.

171
00:08:17.756 --> 00:08:19.431
Is the ID on the access list?

172
00:08:19.456 --> 00:08:21.211
If not, silence.

173
00:08:21.236 --> 00:08:23.731
Is the command status or Relatorio.

174
00:08:23.756 --> 00:08:29.731
If it's any other text, the only reply is unknown command.

175
00:08:29.756 --> 00:08:34.251
And only then does it execute that command's function.

176
00:08:34.276 --> 00:08:38.951
Denise wanted to test Lucia's bot, sent Relatorio, and got nothing

177
00:08:38.976 --> 00:08:39.711
back.

178
00:08:39.736 --> 00:08:43.091
It wasn't a bug, her number wasn't on the list.

179
00:08:43.116 --> 00:08:49.731
With your number in hand, and open the .env and replace 123456789,

180
00:08:49.756 --> 00:08:52.291
which is just the kit's example, with your ID.

181
00:08:52.316 --> 00:08:56.411
For more people, separate the numbers with commas.

182
00:08:56.436 --> 00:08:58.191
But start with just yourself.

183
00:08:58.216 --> 00:09:00.096
Pause the video.

184
00:09:00.156 --> 00:09:05.171
Check that Python 3 is version 3.10 or higher, run identification

185
00:09:05.196 --> 00:09:08.396
mode, write down your number and put it on the list.

186
00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.660
With the list ready, how does the bot keep listening?

187
00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:15.375
With long polling, the program asks Telegram whether a new message

188
00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.440
has arrived.

189
00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:19.620
If not, it waits up to 25 seconds and asks again.

190
00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.255
It's like stopping by your cubby in the teacher's room and

191
00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:24.500
lingering for a moment in case a note shows up.

192
00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:28.455
There's another way, the webhook, which would be the mail carrier

193
00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.060
ringing the doorbell.

194
00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:32.915
Telegram calls an address of yours on the internet, but that

195
00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.680
requires a public address.

196
00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.820
And it isn't used in this module.

197
00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:40.280
Both work, but the kit uses the first one.

198
00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:43.935
Lucia left the bot running on her laptop, at home, and

199
00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:45.920
didn't have to touch any network settings.

200
00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.255
The program goes out to fetch the messages, and nobody needs

201
00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:50.800
to get into her computer.

202
00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:54.895
To start it, in the terminal, in the bot folder, run

203
00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:57.575
python3botpy, no line appears.

204
00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:57.955
And that's the right sign.

205
00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:00.380
The program is waiting.

206
00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:02.080
The terminal has to stay open.

207
00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:06.320
Close the window or press ctrl-c, and the bot stops replying.

208
00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:10.220
Denise found the still screen strange and almost closed it.

209
00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:14.875
Lucia explained, I screen with no new lines is the bot

210
00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:18.246
working, and a new line is usually a warning.

211
00:10:18.506 --> 00:10:22.141
With the bot running, send status and relatorio in the private

212
00:10:22.166 --> 00:10:22.901
chat.

213
00:10:22.926 --> 00:10:25.441
But before you start it, look at the file with the

214
00:10:25.466 --> 00:10:27.786
command cat vendas.csv.

215
00:10:28.986 --> 00:10:32.681
Because afterwards the terminal is busy, Lucia added it up on

216
00:10:32.706 --> 00:10:33.546
paper.

217
00:10:33.726 --> 00:10:36.906
3550 plus 950 plus 55.

218
00:10:37.526 --> 00:10:39.081
That came to 100 reais.

219
00:10:39.106 --> 00:10:41.401
the same number as the bot.

220
00:10:41.426 --> 00:10:44.941
A total that matches the file is a verified result, not

221
00:10:44.966 --> 00:10:46.026
an impression.

222
00:10:46.526 --> 00:10:48.141
One more precaution.

223
00:10:48.166 --> 00:10:51.381
Keep a single program fetching messages for each bot.

224
00:10:51.406 --> 00:10:55.261
Two at the same time, with the same token, compete for

225
00:10:55.286 --> 00:10:57.941
the messages, and Telegram refuses.

226
00:10:57.966 --> 00:11:01.821
The kit notices that conflict and shuts itself down with a

227
00:11:01.846 --> 00:11:04.581
warning in the log, which shows up right in the terminal

228
00:11:04.606 --> 00:11:06.461
without revealing the token.

229
00:11:06.486 --> 00:11:10.941
The warning number is 409, which means conflict.

230
00:11:10.966 --> 00:11:13.861
Lúcia started the bot at home, forgetting it was still running

231
00:11:13.886 --> 00:11:16.421
on the school laptop, and the one at home stopped with

232
00:11:16.446 --> 00:11:17.141
that warning.

233
00:11:17.166 --> 00:11:20.341
The next day, she stopped the one at school and restarted

234
00:11:20.366 --> 00:11:20.971
the one at home.

235
00:11:21.511 --> 00:11:25.486
Now pause the video, add up the sales file on paper,

236
00:11:25.511 --> 00:11:29.786
start the bot, send status and relatório from your phone and

237
00:11:29.811 --> 00:11:30.706
compare the total.

238
00:11:30.731 --> 00:11:34.806
Then press Ctrl C and send status again.

239
00:11:34.831 --> 00:11:37.566
No reply should come.

240
00:11:37.591 --> 00:11:41.026
If the bot replies later when you restart it, that's normal.

241
00:11:41.051 --> 00:11:43.406
The bot works without AI.

242
00:11:43.431 --> 00:11:47.286
So where would the AI come in without spoiling the total.

243
00:11:47.311 --> 00:11:51.646
The kit deliberately separates the message path, which is telegram,

244
00:11:51.671 --> 00:11:52.986
from the work functions.

245
00:11:53.011 --> 00:11:56.946
And it starts with no AI, status, and a report on

246
00:11:56.971 --> 00:11:58.246
fictional data.

247
00:11:58.271 --> 00:12:02.066
A predictable bot is one you can test without spending anything.

248
00:12:02.091 --> 00:12:08.766
Only then is it worth asking whether AI improves interpretation, summarizing,

249
00:12:08.791 --> 00:12:10.346
or classification.

250
00:12:10.371 --> 00:12:14.586
Denise wanted a school office frequently asked questions bot with

251
00:12:14.611 --> 00:12:15.806
AI from the start.

252
00:12:15.831 --> 00:12:17.526
She changed the plan.

253
00:12:17.551 --> 00:12:21.986
First, a horario command for schedules that only reads the spreadsheet

254
00:12:22.011 --> 00:12:25.706
and the AI was left for a second step with testing.

255
00:12:25.731 --> 00:12:30.792
If a new bot already calls an AI for everything, when

256
00:12:30.817 --> 00:12:34.312
it gets something wrong, nobody knows whether it was the program

257
00:12:34.337 --> 00:12:36.152
or the AI.

258
00:12:36.177 --> 00:12:39.632
Step by step, step two is compared with the result of

259
00:12:39.657 --> 00:12:43.252
step one and you investigate one error at a time.

260
00:12:43.277 --> 00:12:47.732
On a report card, the grade comes from the calculation and

261
00:12:47.757 --> 00:12:50.032
the written comment discusses it.

262
00:12:50.057 --> 00:12:53.112
The comment never changes degrade.

263
00:12:53.137 --> 00:12:54.672
It's the same with the bot.

264
00:12:54.697 --> 00:12:57.312
The AI can write a summary, but the total comes from

265
00:12:57.337 --> 00:13:00.192
the program and can't change in the text.

266
00:13:00.217 --> 00:13:04.192
Lucia imagined a resumo command, a summary for the shop.

267
00:13:04.217 --> 00:13:07.672
The AI would receive only the total and the three products,

268
00:13:07.697 --> 00:13:09.417
not the entire folder of her projects.

269
00:13:10.117 --> 00:13:11.632
Look at what happened in the chat.

270
00:13:11.657 --> 00:13:14.632
Given the data and a request for a two-line summary, the

271
00:13:14.657 --> 00:13:18.332
AI wrote that sales added up to about 110 reais.

272
00:13:18.357 --> 00:13:22.492
It made up a total that doesn't exist, and that text

273
00:13:22.517 --> 00:13:24.192
can't go out through the bot.

274
00:13:24.217 --> 00:13:27.852
With the sentence, use only this data, don't change any number

275
00:13:27.877 --> 00:13:31.357
and don't add data, the total came back as 100 reais.

276
00:13:32.317 --> 00:13:35.055
With the planner as the biggest share and no new data.

277
00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:40.335
Before switching on any AI, write the integration contract in five

278
00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:40.680
lines.

279
00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:45.715
The data sent, the available model, the cost limit, the maximum

280
00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:49.155
time, and what happens when the AI fails.

281
00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:52.815
The last line is the one most often forgotten, and it's

282
00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.195
the one that keeps the bot useful even when the AI

283
00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:56.340
doesn't answer.

284
00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:59.395
Denise wrote the one for Horario in five minutes, and on

285
00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:02.515
the failure line she put, Without AI, the bot sends the

286
00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:04.180
spreadsheet row as it is.

287
00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:06.195
The cost and time values are examples.

288
00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.355
You set your own.

289
00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:08.680
And one firm rule.

290
00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:13.100
The message never goes straight to an agent like Codex.

291
00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:16.355
Whoever writes on Telegram can't make an agent act on your

292
00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:17.280
computer.

293
00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:21.495
The AI receives a short input, built by the program, and

294
00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:22.775
returns text.

295
00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:25.815
Pause the video, write your contract, and test in the chat

296
00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:27.420
that the summary keeps the 100 reais.

297
00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:31.335
Before taking the bot anywhere, it's worth proving that it fails

298
00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:31.635
well.

299
00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:34.975
The kit comes with a self-test.

300
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:39.375
The bot runs fake messages against its own rules, with no

301
00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.152
token and no internet.

302
00:14:41.177 --> 00:14:46.152
It covers access, group, unknown command, the sum, and broken sales

303
00:14:46.177 --> 00:14:46.952
files.

304
00:14:46.977 --> 00:14:51.112
The command is python3bot, py, with the self-test option, and the

305
00:14:51.137 --> 00:14:54.572
answer is a single line, starting with OK and mentioning 11

306
00:14:54.597 --> 00:14:55.552
scenarios.

307
00:14:55.577 --> 00:14:58.432
If a long error shows up, some scenario failed.

308
00:14:58.457 --> 00:15:01.972
But watch out, the self-test doesn't prove that your bot talks

309
00:15:01.997 --> 00:15:02.992
to Telegram.

310
00:15:03.017 --> 00:15:06.177
It's simulated, and it goes in the log as simulated.

311
00:15:06.777 --> 00:15:09.232
Denise asked whether Lucia's bot obeyed strangers.

312
00:15:09.257 --> 00:15:13.572
Lucia showed the last line of the self-test and noted that

313
00:15:13.597 --> 00:15:15.137
the real test was still missing.

314
00:15:16.297 --> 00:15:18.917
With someone from outside the list.

315
00:15:19.297 --> 00:15:21.112
It's like a sound check before the parents meeting.

316
00:15:21.137 --> 00:15:23.692
You test the microphone with the auditorium empty.

317
00:15:23.717 --> 00:15:26.592
On Telegram, four real tests are enough.

318
00:15:26.617 --> 00:15:32.392
Your own status, any random sentence, a person who's not on

319
00:15:32.417 --> 00:15:34.132
the list, and the bot switched off.

320
00:15:34.157 --> 00:15:34.692
off.

321
00:15:34.717 --> 00:15:37.932
If the bot still replies while it's off, there's another copy

322
00:15:37.957 --> 00:15:38.532
running somewhere.

323
00:15:38.557 --> 00:15:42.592
Lucia asked Denizzi to send Relatorio.

324
00:15:42.617 --> 00:15:46.392
Nothing came back, as expected, and she wrote down, off the

325
00:15:46.417 --> 00:15:48.535
list, telegram, no reply.

326
00:15:48.755 --> 00:15:52.250
And when something fails, the symptom tells you where to look.

327
00:15:52.275 --> 00:15:53.435
Don't switch the AI model.

328
00:15:54.075 --> 00:15:57.535
Because status and Relatorio don't even use AI.

329
00:15:57.735 --> 00:16:00.715
If only Relatorio fails, the problem is in the sales file.

330
00:16:02.015 --> 00:16:05.370
Lúcia got the message that the file couldn't be validated, and

331
00:16:05.395 --> 00:16:07.730
found out she had deleted the header.

332
00:16:07.755 --> 00:16:12.370
If nothing replies, check the program, the token, the internet, and

333
00:16:12.395 --> 00:16:13.155
the access list.

334
00:16:13.755 --> 00:16:16.835
On a network failure, the bot retries on its own.

335
00:16:16.895 --> 00:16:20.350
On a conflict, the 409, or with the wrong token, the

336
00:16:20.375 --> 00:16:24.095
401, it shuts itself down so you can investigate.

337
00:16:25.015 --> 00:16:27.675
The log shows the type of failure and the time.

338
00:16:28.535 --> 00:16:31.130
But it doesn't show the token or the text of the

339
00:16:31.155 --> 00:16:31.535
messages.

340
00:16:32.195 --> 00:16:35.150
Lucia turned off the Wi-Fi on purpose, with the bot running.

341
00:16:35.175 --> 00:16:39.270
The terminal showed retry warnings, each one waiting twice as long

342
00:16:39.295 --> 00:16:41.610
as the last, and the bot came back on its own

343
00:16:41.635 --> 00:16:42.895
when the network returned.

344
00:16:43.515 --> 00:16:45.835
Pause the video and sound check your bot.

345
00:16:45.875 --> 00:16:47.195
Run the self-test.

346
00:16:47.275 --> 00:16:51.510
Start the bot, send status and any sentence, ask someone off

347
00:16:51.535 --> 00:16:54.787
the list to send the relatorio, and finally, stop it and

348
00:16:54.812 --> 00:16:56.172
confirm the silence.

349
00:16:57.072 --> 00:16:59.272
Mark each line as simulated or telegram.

350
00:16:59.712 --> 00:17:02.587
With no one to help, write not tested.

351
00:17:02.612 --> 00:17:04.552
An honest log is worth more.

352
00:17:05.072 --> 00:17:06.412
Let's put it all together.

353
00:17:06.512 --> 00:17:09.607
Telegram carries messages back and forth, and the one that decides

354
00:17:09.632 --> 00:17:13.167
is your program, which accepts only known commands.

355
00:17:13.192 --> 00:17:17.047
The bot token lives only in the .env protected, and if it

356
00:17:17.072 --> 00:17:19.012
leaks, you revoke and replace it.

357
00:17:19.572 --> 00:17:23.187
The access list says who the bot serves, by number, not

358
00:17:23.212 --> 00:17:24.067
by name.

359
00:17:24.092 --> 00:17:27.107
You start the bot with long polling, check the total against

360
00:17:27.132 --> 00:17:29.292
the file, and keep just one copy running.

361
00:17:30.272 --> 00:17:34.507
AI comes in at one step after the base is tested,

362
00:17:34.532 --> 00:17:37.452
with a five-line contract and the number left untouched.

363
00:17:37.972 --> 00:17:41.727
And you test before you trust, separating what was simulated from

364
00:17:41.752 --> 00:17:44.747
what was real, When you have about 30 minutes, do the

365
00:17:44.772 --> 00:17:47.607
module lab in the supplementary material.

366
00:17:47.632 --> 00:17:53.012
In the next module, VPS from scratch and 24-7 operation.

367
00:17:53.752 --> 00:17:57.892
The bot running all day long without depending on your computer.

368
00:17:58.892 --> 00:17:59.524
See you there.
